    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "The correctness core of our own CNF encoder, stated as a proposition and checked. Not merely equisatisfiable: the clause set is EQUIVALENT to the gate definition, which is the stronger property that makes the encoding model-preserving and so makes model lifting through Tseitin sound. What remains unstated -- and is the real theorem -- is that the recursive Tseitin transformation of an ARBITRARY formula is equisatisfiable with it. That quantifies over formulas; we have no object for a formula, so this single gate is the largest instance we can pin.\n\nOn the axiom footprint: it names the trust base of the SMT ROUTE that established this fact -- the axeyum-ir Boolean evaluator, and the two-valued semantics of the SMT-LIB Bool sort that makes exhaustive truth-table enumeration a proof. It is deliberately NOT empty and deliberately NOT a Lean axiom list. Nothing here went through axeyum's Lean kernel. Measured 2026-08-14 with `cargo run -q -p axeyum-lean-kernel --example nat_axiom_inventory`: the `logic` prelude reports axiom=0 opaque=0 quotient=0, and its declarations are exactly True, False, And, Or, Iff, Not (as `a -> False`), Eq and Exists -- an intuitionistic core with no `Classical.em`, no `propext` and no `Quot.sound`. Zero trusted declarations there means the kernel assumes nothing, not that it can prove everything.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "command": "python3 render/producers-py/facts_to_docir.py",
        "epoch": {
          "commit": "d637d83f77dbfa43c98eee4ab0ad78d235099006",
